Third-party code in this repository
===================================

third_party/public_src/
  Source: anubisyy, "CatBoost-LGBM-NNLS pipeline", Kaggle notebook, 2026.
          https://www.kaggle.com/code/anubisyy/catboost-lgbm-nnls-pipeline-top-50-0-86517
  Use: Task 1 CatBoost residual feature pipeline (prepare_state.py, state_model.py, train_state.py, state_inference.py)
       and Task 2 onset/ongoing feature code (queue_features.py, queue_ongoing.py, train_onset*.py, train_ongoing.py).
       The public queue model files in the weights dataset (models/public_queue/) come from the same notebook.
  Changes: state_inference.py replaced by the notebook's tfb_source version; attribution headers added.

third_party/t2_src/
  Source: yeashusemwal, "TrafficFlowBench Trees + U-Net + CNN", Kaggle notebook, 2026.
          https://www.kaggle.com/code/yeashusemwal/trafficflowbench-trees-u-net-cnn-lb-0-87
  Use: Task 2 ongoing LightGBM ensemble training and inference code (task2_v10/v11/v15/v18, t2_gbm_infer.py), retrained by me.
  Changes: attribution headers added; members retrained with the seeds listed in train/t2_member.py.

Both notebooks were published on Kaggle as public notebooks. Their code is redistributed here, with credit, so that the
solution can be reproduced. The licence terms are those stated on each notebook's Kaggle page.

Organisers' code
  TrafficFlowBench (J. Wu), https://github.com/jacky850/trafficflowbench-public : data release, scoring specification and scorers.
  The scoring re-implementations in tfb/t1_common.py follow docs/SCORING_SPEC.md of that repository.

Everything else (tfb/, train/, experiments/, eda/, kaggle/) is my own work (Homeshwar Nelakurthi).
